## Task Manager App (js/apps/taskmanager.js)

### All translations added to en.js
- File: `js/i18n/en.js` (lines 245-268)
- Namespace: `taskmanager.*`
- All user-facing strings are properly localized
- No hardcoded strings found

**Translation keys:**
- `taskmanager.title` - 'Task Manager'
- `taskmanager.description` - 'View and manage running applications and windows. Monitor system resources.'
- `taskmanager.windows` - 'Windows'
- `taskmanager.systemInfo` - 'System Information'
- `taskmanager.refresh` - 'Refresh'
- `taskmanager.noWindows` - 'No windows are currently open'
- `taskmanager.statusBarReady` - 'Ready'
- `taskmanager.statusRunning` - 'Running'
- `taskmanager.statusMinimized` - 'Minimized'
- `taskmanager.switchTo` - 'Switch To'
- `taskmanager.endTask` - 'End Task'
- `taskmanager.endTaskConfirm` - 'End task "{title}"?' (with placeholder)
- `taskmanager.columnApp` - 'App'
- `taskmanager.columnTitle` - 'Window Title'
- `taskmanager.columnStatus` - 'Status'
- `taskmanager.columnSize` - 'Size'
- `taskmanager.columnMemory` - 'Memory'
- `taskmanager.columnActions` - 'Actions'
- `taskmanager.totalWindows` - 'Total Windows'
- `taskmanager.runningWindows` - 'Running'
- `taskmanager.minimizedWindows` - 'Minimized'
- `taskmanager.totalMemory` - 'Total Memory'
- `taskmanager.systemUptime` - 'System Uptime'
- `taskmanager.browserInfo` - 'Browser'

**Context:**
- Task Manager is a system utility app for viewing and managing open windows
- Hidden from desktop and start menu, accessible only via search
- Shows window list with app name, title, status, size, memory usage
- Shows system information (total windows, memory, uptime)
- Allows switching to windows and ending tasks

## Dialog Framework (js/core.dialog.js)

### All translations added to en.js
- File: `js/i18n/en.js` (lines 333-340)
- Namespace: `dialog.*`
- All user-facing strings are properly localized
- No hardcoded strings found

**Translation keys:**
- `dialog.alert` - 'Alert' (default title for alert dialogs)
- `dialog.confirm` - 'Confirm' (default title for confirmation dialogs)
- `dialog.prompt` - 'Prompt' (default title for prompt dialogs)
- `dialog.ok` - 'OK' (button label for OK/Confirm actions)
- `dialog.cancel` - 'Cancel' (button label for Cancel actions)
- `dialog.yes` - 'Yes' (button label, currently unused but available)
- `dialog.no` - 'No' (button label, currently unused but available)

**Context:**
- Dialog framework replaces native browser `alert()`, `prompt()`, and `confirm()` dialogs
- Used throughout the OS for user interactions (file operations, confirmations, input prompts)
- All dialogs are Promise-based and async/await compatible
- Keyboard shortcuts: Enter to confirm, Escape to cancel
- Fully themed to match OS appearance
- **NEW**: Added `Dialog.saveAs()` and `Dialog.open()` with file browser navigation

**Files using dialog framework:**
- `js/core.filesave.js` - Save As and Open dialogs (now with file browser), error alerts
- `js/core.shell.js` - Desktop folder creation prompts and alerts
- `js/apps/files.js` - File/folder operations, delete confirmations, error alerts
- `js/apps/taskmanager.js` - End task confirmations
- `js/apps/settings.js` - Reset file system confirmations, wallpaper error alerts
- `js/apps/draw.js` - New drawing confirmations, about dialog

## File Browser Component (js/core.filebrowser.js)

### New reusable component
- File: `js/core.filebrowser.js` (new)
- Provides common file/folder navigation UI
- Used by `Dialog.saveAs()` and `Dialog.open()` dialogs
- Can be reused by Files app (future refactoring)

**Translation keys used:**
- `files.emptyFolder` - 'This folder is empty' (already exists)
- `files.fileName` - 'File' (already exists, used as label)
- `files.size` - 'Size' (added to `files.*` namespace)
- `files.deleteFile` - 'Delete' (already exists)
- `files.up` - 'Up' (already exists)
- `common.error` - 'Error' (already exists)

**Context:**
- Common component for rendering file/folder lists
- Supports list and grid view modes
- Handles file icons, sizes, and selection
- Supports filtering (files only, folders only, or both)
- Used in Save As and Open dialogs for navigation

